{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation of #10952 at internal/app@f24f2a8c55314908a36d1875c4f39b102c31732c on branch request/mcp-late-actor-resolution (worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/mcp-late-actors), recut onto current main 6fad9e8a6. Workspace.ResolveActor answers from the in-memory custody view first (zero filesystem cost); only a miss takes one serialised fresh read of config.json and adopts it on success, so an actor another process adds after the workspace opened resolves without reopening. The two failures stay apart: still-unknown after a successful fresh read says \"addresses no known actor\", an unreadable custody record reports its own I/O failure. Chosen shape is re-read-on-resolution-miss rather than config-change detection or dropping the cache: misses are rare and share one serialised read, so the hot path stays memory-only. Verification at this exact head: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -race -count=1 ./internal/app ./cmd/gitseq-mcp green; mutation proofs run by me — removing the re-read/adoption guard alone fails TestResolveActorFindsActorAddedAfterOpen, collapsing the I/O branch into the unknown wording alone fails TestResolveActorErrorCasesStayApart. Honest suite caveat: in full `go test ./... -count=1` runs, cmd/gitseq-mcp's TestCredentialsArePerRepositoryAndAbsentFromToolResultsAndURLs flakes under parallel load, reproduced identically on unmodified main 6fad9e8a6 (full-suite baseline) and under a matched contention probe on both heads, and passes package-alone on both; two whoami timing tests failed only in full-suite runs at this head and pass alone, under -race, and under the matched probe on both heads.","body":{"area":"internal/app","branch":"request/mcp-late-actor-resolution","commit":"f24f2a8c55314908a36d1875c4f39b102c31732c","head":"f24f2a8c55314908a36d1875c4f39b102c31732c","path":"internal/app"}}